    "attributes": "Source is nonmutating. Extracted masks are zero; source RGB is retained at originals and interpolated along cuts. New part has no layers, target or levels.",
    "clipping": "Ordered triangles clipped at linear mask >= threshold. f64 canonical edge interpolation rounded to f32; exact-threshold intersections use original endpoint IDs. Zero-area point/edge touches are discarded.",
    "normal": "Corner-angle-weighted f64 geometric normals computed from the selected rounded patch. Stored source normals are ignored; source winding defines outward. Every incident face must see positive normal/rounded outward displacement.",
    "precision": "Every source/clipped/outer/side face must be finite and nonzero area; clip and extrusion orientations must remain positive relative to their local expected face directions. f32 thickness collapse/world overflow rejects.",
    "shell": "Reversed original inner skin, same-winding outer skin displaced by thickness, two outward side triangles per boundary edge. Closed patches can form two disconnected nested closed surfaces.",
